# Banners

Banner art lives in `assets/banners/`. When Geo says "use a banner", use these files. Don't draw a banner with `clip-path` or hand-made SVG.

## Kingdom banners

Use these when the banner stands for a specific kingdom. The colors are baked into the art, so don't tint them.

| Kingdom | File | Fill |
|---|---|---|
| Emberhold | `emberhold.svg` | `#D43F3C` |
| Thornwald | `thornwald.svg` | `#7B9953` |
| Solmere | `solmere.svg` | `#DD9E40` |
| Tidereach | `tidereach.svg` | `#508FC7` |

## General banners

`general-1.svg`, `general-2.svg` and `general-3.svg` are white silhouettes for anything not tied to a kingdom, such as game modes or decoration. Pick any one; varying them across a row is fine. Tint them with a CSS mask so the color comes from the surrounding UI:

```css
.banner-art{
  background:var(--c);
  -webkit-mask:url("assets/banners/general-2.svg") center/contain no-repeat;
          mask:url("assets/banners/general-2.svg") center/contain no-repeat;
}
```

All banners have a ragged bottom edge. Keep the file's aspect ratio (kingdom 94×153, general about 63×103) and don't stretch them.
